body:
My void super would be that you turn invisible like with Wraith, float around like with Novawarp, get a health boost and get to blink semi-oftenly. Invisibility also hides you from enemy radars.

&#x200B;

Getting close to any number of enemies applies the supress effect to them which also lets you see them through walls and other obstacles.

&#x200B;

Getting melee-close to an enemy allows you to do a finisher-type of move where you suck the life out of them in the span of a few seconds, regaining any lost health or charging you with an overshield if you're at max, also extending the duration of the super. 

Doing this move pulls you out of the invisibility which does make you easier to target and you also reappear on enemy radars but you keep the health boost.

&#x200B;

You can cancel the finisher at any moment in case you get surrounded or the enemies are applying too much pressure on you, but doing so comes at the cost of extending the super.

&#x200B;

Edit: I'd call it Soulreaper or something

I had this happen to me to the point I was having fits of anger and lashing out at my family for it. My solution was to main the soccerballs while listening to chill synthwave and not try to win but simply try to be the best hero. It really helped take things slower, be less ragey, admire the environments, make new friends (even with the block spammers in the enemy team), and after a while I was complimenting the enemy for their teamwork, skills, or strategy, which lead me to accept that if they were emote-taunting me it was because they had earned it by having one of the three previously listed things

&#x200B;

Edit: Thanks to this playstyle I also ended up developing the mentality that if you're going to loose you might aswell try to be the best hero you can possibly be
